From 85fe64af857d0679d1425f8a51724751d4402090 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@example.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 16:40:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Stride walk: survivor queues without full-plane or lane-0
 assumptions

The nice-only stride kernel queues its cross filter's survivors in shared
memory and checks them in dense waves. Both queues assumed full planes laid
out along UNIT_POS_X: the plane-scoped queue drained PLANE_DIM entries per
wave through lanes UNIT_POS_X % PLANE_DIM and placed each plane's queue at
PLANE_POS * 2 * PLANE_DIM; the cube-scoped queue had lane 0 publish each
plane's total at UNIT_POS_X / PLANE_DIM and summed CUBE_DIM_X / PLANE_DIM
of them. On a partly filled plane survivors were dropped unchecked.

Now only the lanes that run decide: ranks, counts and takes come from a
ballot (planes of at most 32 lanes) or a scan over the running lanes, the
plane-scoped queue's slots are reserved by each plane's lowest running lane
from a cube counter, and the cube-scoped queue's planes reserve their
offsets with one shared atomic per plane. Each cube counts survivors queued
minus checked (and the same for their low words) and the host fails the
field unless both are zero.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
